  "configuration_id": "config_041",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_003 (scgpt + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted) achieved the best accuracy (0.542) at low cost (2.94 GPU hrs), clearly outperforming config_009 (same architecture but concat fusion, acc=0.518, cost=7.18). This establishes weighted fusion as superior and identifies scgpt/imagenet_vit_l as a strong backbone. Uncertainty: we have only tested avgpool aggregation; transformer aggregation could capture richer inter-profile interactions that avgpool discards. This experiment (config_041) tests transformer aggregation while holding all other proven components constant (scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, weighted fusion, multiprofile), making it a clean single-variable extension of our best result. It is the best use of experiment 3 because: (1) it directly exploits the strongest evidence while probing the most impactful untested design axis (aggregation), (2) a positive result would give a clear exploitation path for remaining budget, and (3) a negative result would confirm avgpool sufficiency and redirect exploration toward RNA/image encoder choices. Expected relative cost: moderate (~4-6 GPU hrs), higher than avgpool due to attention computation but well below the concat-fusion overhead seen in config_009."
}

